{"content":{"result":[{"rank_order":1,"title":"Customer Carbon Footprint Tool","context":"# Customer Carbon Footprint Tool\n\n**Carbon emissions data**\n\nThe Customer Carbon Footprint Tool gives you an overview of the estimated carbon emissions\nassociated with\nyour usage of AWS services.\n\nCarbon emissions data is available for the previous 38 months. New data is available\nmonthly and usually published between the 15th ‐ 21st of the month after the usage\noccurs. In the Customer Carbon Footprint Tool, emissions are shown at the 0.001 MTCO2e\n(1kgCO2e) resolution. If your emissions are lower than 0.0005 MTCO2e (0.5 kgCO2e),\nit will be appear as `zero`. To see your carbon footprint at the 0.000001 MTCO2e (1 gram) resolution, use **AWS Data Exports**.\n\n**AWS management account users**\n\nIf you're using a management account, the Customer Carbon Footprint Tool dashboard\nand downloadable report shows the consolidated member account data. This only includes\nthe duration these accounts are a part of your organization.\n\nTo learn more about historical changes to the features, methodology, and other\ninformation, see the *Customer Carbon Footprint Tool Release Notes*","url":"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/help-panel/awsaccountbilling/latest/console/hp-ccft.html"},{"rank_order":2,"title":"Carbon emissions","context":"# Carbon emissions\n\nThe carbon emissions page enables you to visualize and understand the estimated carbon\nemissions associated\nwith your usage of AWS services.\n\nCarbon emissions data is available from January 2022. New data is available monthly\nand usually published\nbetween the 15th ‐ 21st of the month after the usage occurs. Emissions are shown at\nthe 0.000001 MTCO2e (1\ngram) resolution.\n\nTo get your data in bulk, visit Reports.\n\n**AWS management account users**\n\nIf you're using a management account, the dashboard shows the consolidated member\naccount data. This only\nincludes the duration these accounts are a part of your organization.\n\nTo learn more about historical changes to AWS Sustainability's features, methodology,\nand more, see\nRelease notes","url":"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/help-panel/sustainability/latest/console/hp-carbon-emissions-main.html"},{"rank_order":3,"title":"Customer Carbon Footprint Tool Release Notes","context":"##### Emissions threshold updated for granularity and expanded historical data\n\nThe CCFT now shows emissions data at a more granular level with expanded historical coverage. Previously, data was not visible if estimated emissions for the AWS account didn't exceed 0.05 MTCO2e over a 36 month period. Now, estimated emissions is visible in the CCFT console and CSV download as long as emissions for any period rounds to 1 kg (0.001 MTCO2e). CCFT console or CSV download will show `0 emissions` for the selected time period if the estimated emissions are below 0.0005 MTCO2e. With this update, the CCFT console and CSV download contains 38 months of data instead of the previous 36 months.\n\n**Note:**\n\nData Export continues to display emissions at gram (0.000001 MTCO2e) resolution","url":"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/ccft/latest/releasenotes/what-is-ccftrn.html"}]}}

