d analysis in AWS GovCloud (US-East) and AWS GovCloud (US-West) regions. This feature helps database administrators and developers optimize database performance by providing insights into database metrics, query analysis, and resource utilization patterns. Previously, database administrators had to manually analyze performance data and investigate root causes, which was time-consuming and required deep database expertise. With this launch, users can analyze database performance monitoring data for any time period using automated intelligence. The feature compares the selected time period against normal baseline performance, identifies anomalies, and provides specific remediation advice. The automated analysis and recommendation system reduces mean-time-to-diagnosis from hours to minutes. Users can enable the Advanced mode of CloudWatch Database Insights on their Amazon Aurora and Amazon RDS databases using various methods, including the RDS service console, AWS APIs, the AWS SDK, or AWS CloudFormation","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/03/amazon-cloudwatch-database-insights-on-demand-analysis-in-govcloud/"},{"rank_order":5,"title":"aws-observability","skill_description":"Investigates root causes on the Omni context graph (service dependencies) and Intelligence insights; builds, configures, debugs, tunes AWS observability - operator-symptom questions, detecting Omni vs classic CloudWatch. CloudWatch on a reporting service: fleet health views, Log Insights, metric/composite/anomaly alarms, custom metrics/EMF, dashboards, X-Ray/ADOT tracing, canaries, CloudTrail, Dynamic Instrumentation (live breakpoints), and Application Signals service map. CloudWatch Omni on an existing Space: SQL over logs/traces, PromQL, Omni dashboards, alerts and Slack notifications, programmatic/IaC access (API/SDK/CLI/CFN), driving Omni from a coding agent or skills, AI agent quality from traces - on-demand and online evaluation of live traffic, incl. setting it up, readback, evaluators. For first-time setup - creating an Omni Space, granting access, ingestion, or ADOT instrumentation for Application Signals or Omni - use setting-up-cloudwatch-observability. Not for app logging or threat detection.\n\nServices: cloudwatch, cloudwatch-omni, xray, cloudtrail, synthetics, application-signals\nTasks: build, deploy, debug, optimize, configure, enable, onboard, instrument, query\nPersona: developer, devops\nWorkload: observability\n*","skill_name":"aws-observability"}]}}"}]}], "label": "Look up AWS docs on carbon footprint tool data latency and availability"}

